  "query_preview": "..\nCoverage remains isolated at this hour, but there should be an \nuptick in activity through the afternoon. Main TS risks for \ntoday are gusty outflow winds to 35 mph+, lightning, and heavy \nrain. There could be some nuisance flooding this afternoon into \nearly evening, but nothing widespread expected. WPC maintains a \nMarginal Risk for Excessive Rainfall today. \n\nWed/Thu look to be more active as high pressure elongates west\nto east across central AZ/NM brining modest SE/E flow to the\nregion. This will aid in storm development with plenty of \nmoisture and instability around. WPC has bumped up SEAZ to a \nSlight Risk for Excessive Rainfall, which aligns well with \nCAMs. While severe probabilities are low at this time, with the\nincreased flow there should be at least some organization into \nthe lower deserts. This should help some of the stronger storms \nto have wind speeds eclipsing 50 mph with small hail. Isolated \ninstances of flash flooding will also be possible both days.  \n\nWhile activity trends down into the weekend, enough \nmoisture/instability will remain for daily shower/storm \nchances. They will generally favor areas south and east of \nTucson.",
